  "description": {
    "text": "Pikachu World (ポケモンカードゲーム ピカチュウ ワールド), a binder of nine holo Pikachu cards released in Japan on 8 July 2010 with Clash at the Summit. Each card is printed in a different language, for nine countries: the United States, Italy, Korea, Spain, Japan, Germany, France, Poland and Portugal. Eight show Pikachu in a scene from their country; the Japanese card has Ken Sugimori's Pikachu on a plain holo background.\n\nIt came in two binders: a blue one sold at Pokémon Centers and a green one sold only at 7-Eleven stores. They differ in the Japanese card alone, whose background is green in the 7-Eleven binder. In November 2010 the same nine cards came to the US in a box with the 2010 World Championships decks, with English backs and a shorter copyright line, ©2010 Pokémon/Nintendo in place of the binders' ©2010 Pokémon/Nintendo/Creatures/GAME FREAK.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "PocketMonsters.net: Pokémon Card Game Pikachu World Set (2010)",
